CREATE FUNCTION my_func()
RETURNS BIGINT
DETERMINISTIC
BEGIN ATOMIC
DECLARE seq_val BIGINT;
SELECT NEXTVAL FOR my_sequence INTO seq_val;
RETURN seq_val;
END;

This function will obtain the next value from the specified sequence (my_sequence) and return it. You can then use this function in your SELECT or INSERT statements as shown in your example.

Please note that the function is marked as DETERMINISTIC, which means that for the same input parameters, the function will always return the same output. However, since we are not passing any parameters and the sequence value can change, this might not be strictly accurate. If you encounter issues with this, you may need to remove the DETERMINISTIC keyword.

Also, the BEGIN ATOMIC clause ensures that the function will be executed as an atomic unit, which means it will either complete successfully or fail completely, without leaving the database in an inconsistent state.

Remember to replace "my_sequence" with the actual name of your sequence in the database.

