for (int i=0,n=v.size()-1; i<n; i++)
{
    total += v[i] + foo();
}

This way the elements of the vector are more likely to be in the same cache line and you may get a speedup. If this trick works then you may want to look into using a different data structure that is more cache friendly (like a block vector or a matrix).

