To solve this issue, you need to configure your Nginx server to serve the static files for all routes. This can be done by adding a location block in your Nginx configuration file. Here is an example configuration:

```nginx
location / {
    try_files $uri /index.html;
    root /path/to/your/build/directory;
}
```

This configuration tells Nginx to first try to serve the requested file directly. If the file is not found, it will serve the index.html file from the root directory. This way, all routes will be handled by your React app, and you won't get a 404 error.

