However, if two elements have the same gsize, we want to sort them by glow, smallest to largest. To achieve this, we can modify the sort function to include the glow comparison. Here is the updated function:

grouperArray.sort(function (a, b) {
    var aSize = a.gsize;
    var bSize = b.gsize;
    var aLow = a.glow;
    var bLow = b.glow;
    var sizeComparison = (aSize < bSize) ? -1 : (aSize > bSize) ? 1 : 0;
    var glowComparison = (aLow < bLow) ? -1 : (aLow > bLow) ? 1 : 0;
    return sizeComparison || glowComparison;
});

This code first compares the gsize of the elements. If they are equal, it then compares the glow of the elements. The result is a sorted array where elements are first sorted by gsize and then by glow.

